{"node_id": "NRS_484B_257_1_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-257-1"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "When proper signs have been erected,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall stop or yield", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "at a clearly marked stop line", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "or, if there is none, then at the point nearest the intersection", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "After having stopped or, in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "the driver shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "to other vehicles which have entered the intersection from such through highway", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "or which are approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "dev.human_direction", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.inoperative", "dev.governs", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic; the traffic whose control matters is the subject's own flow, so x is read as a member. 'being controlled by a police officer' is dev.human_direction 'a person directing traffic' with role police_officer (DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic') governing the intersection or x's approach carrier (dev.governs); 'or a traffic-control signal' is a dev.traffic_signal governing them that is not dev.inoperative ('showing no valid indication'): a dark signal controls nothing, and NRS 484B.250(4) then governs."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'proper signs' are dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt') or dev.yield_sign ('regulatory sign requiring yielding without a mandatory halt') governing (dev.governs) x's approach carrier c (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters c i) or the intersection; the duty is owed on the approach to x's entry into the intersection (drv.motion.entering_region)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'the driver' is read through its controlled motion."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["kin.speed", "kin.velocity", "kin.heading", "kin.accel_longitudinal"], "derived": ["drv.motion.halted", "drv.motion.slowing"], "justification": "'stop' (required: DEF-NRS-484A-255 'complete cessation from movement') is drv.motion.halted; 'or yield' at a yield sign is, by the words of the next sentence ('in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped'), a halt or slowing (drv.motion.slowing: forward motion with kin.accel_longitudinal below minus the resolution). kin.accel_longitudinal is not a stand-in for speed; both are read."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.stop_line", "st.entrance_of", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: st.stop_line recorded by st.entrance_of as marking x's approach carrier; nearness by st.region_geometry, side by prim.region_offset_along along the carrier's direction."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "st.entrance_of", "rel.occupies", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: the st.crosswalk st.entrance_of records as marking x's approach carrier, with the halt's footprint not overlapping it (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["st.intersection", "rel.occupies", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: footprint outside the intersection, distance by st.region_geometry."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s8", "standard": "a view of approaching traffic on the through highway: how much of the through highway must be in view", "concepts": ["st.sight_along_way", "st.highway", "st.on_way"], "params": ["p.intersection_sight_distance"], "convention": "Intersection sight distance for a stop- or yield-controlled approach (AASHTO Green Book cases B and C): from the place of the act, the through highway (a st.highway on which the intersection lies, st.on_way, and the subject's approach carrier does not) is in view for at least p.intersection_sight_distance (st.sight_along_way, the smaller of its two directions); not a stand-in for whether an actual road user is seen.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) through an approach carrier c it occupies (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c i); a dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governs c or i (dev.governs) at this observation; and traffic is not being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal: x being a member of traffic (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic), no dev.human_direction with role police_officer and no dev.traffic_signal that is not dev.inoperative governs c or i at this observation. Where x occupies several carriers entering i and the verdict differs between them, which governs is unknown.", "obligation": "Act: where a dev.stop_sign governs c or i, x halted (drv.motion.halted x with p.speed_resolution) at the place; where only a dev.yield_sign governs, x halted at the place or was slowing (drv.motion.slowing x with p.speed_resolution and p.deceleration_resolution) at some observation of the approach before passing the place (before the place is behind x along c by prim.region_offset_along; for place (3), before x enters i). Place, in the words' order: (1) where a stop line s (st.stop_line) is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of s c): at s, x's body within p.stop_point_tolerance of s (st_region_geometry_distance) and s not behind x along c (prim.region_offset_along x s c at least zero); (2) where the source observes that no stop line marks c and a crosswalk w is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of w c): before entering w, x's footprint not overlapping w, within p.stop_point_tolerance of w and w ahead along c; (3) where the source observes that neither marks c: x's footprint outside i, within p.stop_point_tolerance of i, or farther upstream where a highway h on which i lies and c does not (st.on_way i h; st.on_way c h false) is in view from x for at least p.intersection_sight_distance (st_sight_along_way x h). History bound (the approach convention): the search runs back from this entry to the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which x, on c, is outside the governing place's stopping zone upstream (not on it, short of it along c, farther than p.stop_point_tolerance), or to x's previous entry into i, whichever is later; the act found there meets the duty, reaching either end without it violates it, reaching neither leaves it unknown. An act before the previous entry into i 