proach carrier does not lie on; its designation is presumed from the sign on the subject's approach.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "dev.stop_sign governs lane c (st.lane_enters c i); stop line s marks c; no officer and no signal. x is first observed 80 m upstream at 12 m/s, never falls to the speed resolution and enters i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x halts with its body 0.5 m short of s, then enters i."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "No sign governs c or i; x enters i without halting."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but dev.governs is not observed for the stop sign.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "dev.yield_sign governs c; x, moving forward at 10 m/s, decelerates at 2 m/s² 30 m upstream of s and enters i at 4 m/s without halting."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, but a dev.human_direction with role police_officer governs i while x rolls through."}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but the recording begins with x 1.5 m short of s at 1 m/s; no halt is recorded before x enters i.", "boundary": "x's approach start on c, the last observation outside the stopping zone upstream of s, lies before the recording."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.deceleration_resolution", "unit": "m/s²", "value": 0.3, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest longitudinal deceleration the acquisition standard separates from steady speed; a deceleration at or below it counts as no slowing.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: acceleration resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.stop_point_tolerance", "unit": "m", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Stop-point tolerance: the largest ground distance between a halted body and the line, crossing or intersection edge at which the halt counts as made at that place; a body farther upstream is outside the stopping zone.", "source": "MUTCD 2009 section 3B.16 stop-line placement (at least 4 ft ahead of the crosswalk) and vehicle positioning variability at a stop"}, {"name": "p.intersection_sight_distance", "unit": "m", "value": 100, "convention": "Intersection sight distance: the length of the crossing way, in the smaller of its two directions, that a driver halted on a stop-controlled approach must be able to see to judge a gap in approaching traffic.", "source": "AASHTO A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets (2018) section 9.5.3, case B departure sight triangles at a low urban design speed"}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_257_1_o2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-257-1"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "When proper signs have been erected,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall stop or yield", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "at a clearly marked stop line", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "or, if there is none, then at the point nearest the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "After having stopped or, in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "the driver shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "to other vehicles which have entered the intersection from such through highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "or which are approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "dev.human_direction", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.inoperative", "dev.governs", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_257_1_o1: x as a member of the admitted traffic aggregate; a dev.human_direction with role police_officer, or a dev.traffic_signal not dev.inoperative, governing x's approach carrier or the intersection (dev.governs)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_257_1_o1: a dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governing x's approach carrier or the intersection, at x's entry (drv.motion.entering_region)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate; 'the driver' is read through its controlled motion."}, {"span": "s10", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'shall yield the right-of-way' (DEF-NRS-484A-210 'to proceed ... in preference to another vehicle'): x does not enter the intersection (drv.motion.entering_region over rel.occupies) while a through-highway vehicle is owed precedence."}, {"span": "s11", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": ["drv.position.entered_via"], "justification": "'other vehicles' are the admitted aggregate. 'which have entered the intersection from such through highway': y occupies the intersection, having entered it through a carrier (drv.position.entered_via, st.lane_enters) that lies on the through highway (st.on_way 'the public way ... a structure region lies on', of kind st.highway) on which x's approach carrier does not lie."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s12", "standard": "approaching so closely on the through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard during the time the driver is moving across or within the intersection", "concepts": ["st.region_geometry", "kin.speed", "rel.occupies", "st.lane_enters", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "params": ["p.immediate_hazard_gap"], "convention": "Gap acceptance (HCM critical headway for a minor-street crossing or turn): a vehicle on an approach carrie