d by the entry into or the exit from the controlled-access region it leads to.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "intention"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "The yield is judged at the entry or exit observation: making it while a hazard exists is the failure to yield.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x moves from an on-ramp into controlled-access region a (entering) at 15 m/s while vehicle y in a, 15 m behind and moving at 25 m/s on a converging path, is predicted to come within 1 m of x in 1.5 s."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x enters a as the only road user in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "x drives on an arterial roadway; no st.controlled_access region is entered or left."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but kin.speed of y is not observed.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x enters a while y in a is 300 m behind at 25 m/s: no predicted conflict within the horizon."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.immediate_hazard_gap", "unit": "s", "value": 4.1, "convention": "Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.", "source": "HCM 7th ed. Exhibit 20-11 base critical headway (major-street left turn)"}, {"name": "p.conflict_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.", "source": "FHWA Surrogate Safety Assessment Model (Gettman et al. 2008) conflict definition"}], "gaps": []}
