 directs, through the carriers they approach through: x's approach carrier and the carrier y entered through (drv.position.entered_via) have opposed designated directions (drv.road.opposed_directions over st.lane_direction). rel.oncoming is not used: a turn makes current headings cease to be opposed while the approach direction is unchanged."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"], "justification": "'is making a left turn': the vehicle's heading change since it entered the intersection (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, left positive, integrated from kin.yaw_rate) is at least the turn recognition angle; a bend of the way inside the region also changes it, which a right-angled junction does not offer."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "s8", "id": "int.left_turn", "meaning": "The source's current plan for the road user includes a left turn at the target region."}], "compositions": [{"span": "s5", "rule": "NRS_484B_250_4_o1", "map": {"x": "x"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "s6"}], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) from an approach carrier c it occupies (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c i). Device exception (s6): the duty does not apply where some dev.traffic_signal, dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governs i or c (dev.governs) at this observation; this exception is suspended where NRS_484B_250_4_o1 applies to x here (ruleApplies NRS_484B_250_4_o1 {x -> x}: an entry under an inoperative signal).", "obligation": "At this entry no vehicle y other than x (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) occupies i having entered it from a different highway: y occupies i, entered it through a carrier c2 (drv.position.entered_via y i c2, st.lane_enters c2 i) that lies on a highway h2 (st.highway, st.on_way c2 h2) on which c does not lie (st.on_way c h2 false). Pair exception (s7 to s9): a y is excluded where c and c2 have opposed designated directions (drv.road.opposed_directions c c2 with p.opposed_carriers_cosine) and x or y intends a left turn at i (intent int.left_turn x i, or intent int.left_turn y i) or is making one (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry of x or of y and i, with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph, at least p.turn_recognition_angle).", "params": ["p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_recognition_angle"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "The yield is judged at x's entry into the intersection: an entry while a vehicle from a different highway is in it is the failure to yield.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "'official' is read through the device's presence; the devices that control an intersection are read as traffic signals, stop signs and yield signs governing the intersection or the subject's approach (a marking or a warning sign alone controls no right-of-way there).", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "No device governs i or its approaches. Vehicle y entered i from carrier c2 on highway h2; x, on carrier c on highway h (c not on h2), enters i while y occupies i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x waits on c until y has left i and enters i as the only road user in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A dev.stop_sign governs c; signals are absent; x enters i while y occupies i."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but rel.occupies of y and i is not observed at x's entry.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A dev.traffic_signal governing i is dev.inoperative (NRS_484B_250_4_o1 applies); y entered i from a different highway; x enters i while y occupies it."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "At a skewed junction, y entered i through c2 on another highway whose designated direction is opposed to c's, and int.left_turn y i is declared; x enters while y is in i: the pair is excepted."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.7, "convention": "Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.", "source": "Junction geometry: approaches meeting at an intersection skewed by up to 45 degrees (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9)"}, {"name": "p.turn_recognition_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 45, "convention": "Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.", "source": "Geometry of a right-angled junction (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9 intersection angles)"}], "gaps": []}
