5", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the vehicle making the left turn': the vehicle y (admitted aggregate) in the intersection that s11 reads as making the turn."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "s3", "id": "int.left_turn", "meaning": "The source's current plan for the road user includes a left turn at the target region."}], "compositions": [{"span": "s8", "rule": "NRS_484B_253_o1", "map": {"x": "y"}, "as": "compliance"}], "residues": [{"span": "s10", "why": "'when and as required' refers to the signalling requirements of a law outside this corpus (no bracketed id resolves it); the signal itself is read on s9."}], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) from an approach carrier c it occupies (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c i).", "obligation": "At this entry no vehicle y other than x (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) is making a left turn in i under the words' conditions: y occupies i, having entered it through a carrier c2 (drv.position.entered_via y i c2, st.lane_enters c2 i) with drv.road.opposed_directions c c2 (p.opposed_carriers_cosine); the source declares int.left_turn y i; y is making the turn (drv.motion.turning_left y with p.speed_resolution and p.yaw_rate_resolution, or drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry y i with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph at least p.turn_recognition_angle); y has so yielded (rule NRS_484B_253_o1 {x -> y} complied with at every observation since y's current overlap of i began); and y has given a signal (sig.turn_indicator left, or sig.hand_signal left) at some observation since y last came onto c2 while it has stayed on c2 or in i since.", "params": ["p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "p.speed_resolution", "p.yaw_rate_resolution", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_recognition_angle"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'the driver' of the turning vehicle is read through its controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s12", "why": "'the drivers' are read through the vehicles' controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s14", "why": "The yield is judged at x's entry into the intersection while the turning vehicle is in it.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "y entered i through c2 with sig.turn_indicator left on c2, int.left_turn y i declared, waited in i while no opposing vehicle was near, and now turns left (kin.yaw_rate 15 deg/s, 4 m/s); x on c (opposed to c2) enters i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x waits on c and enters i after y has left it, as the only road user in i."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "x drives along a road segment and enters no intersection."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but neither sig.turn_indicator nor sig.hand_signal of y is observed.", "masked": ["sig.turn_indicator", "sig.hand_signal"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but y's sig.turn_indicator is off and sig.hand_signal no_signal at every observation: y gave no signal, and x owes it no precedence under this duty."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but y began its turn while x was 15 m from i at 15 m/s on c, so NRS_484B_253_o1 was not complied with by y: y has not so yielded."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.7, "convention": "Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.", "source": "Junction geometry: approaches meeting at an intersection skewed by up to 45 degrees (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9)"}, {"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.yaw_rate_resolution", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest yaw rate the acquisition standard separates from a straight path; a yaw rate at or below it counts as no heading change.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: yaw-rate resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.turn_recognition_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 45, "convention": "Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.", "source": "Geometry of a right-angled junction (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9 intersection angles)"}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_257_1_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-257-1"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "When proper signs have been erected,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall stop or yield", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "at a clearly marked stop line", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "or, if there is none, then at the point nearest the intersection", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "After having stopped or, in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "the driver shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "to other vehicles which have entered the intersection from such through highway", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "or which are approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "dev.human_direction", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.inoperative", "dev.governs", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic; the traffic whose control matters is the subject's own flow, so x is read as a member. 'being controlled by a police officer' is dev.human_direction 'a person directing traffic' with role police_officer (DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic') governing the intersection or x's approach carrier (dev.governs); 'or a traffic-control signal' is a dev.traffic_signal governing them that is not dev.inoperative ('showing no valid indication'): a dark signal controls nothing, and NRS 484B.250(4) then governs."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'proper signs' are dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt') or dev.yield_sign ('regulatory sign requiring yielding without a mandatory halt') governing (dev.governs) x's approach carrier c (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters c i) or the intersection; the duty is owed on the approach to x's entry into the intersection (drv.motion.entering_region)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'the driver' is read through its controlled motion."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["kin.speed", "kin.velocity", "kin.heading", "kin.accel_longitudinal"], "derived": ["drv.motion.halted", "drv.motion.slowing"], "justification": "'stop' (required: DEF-NRS-484A-255 'complete cessation from movement') is drv.motion.halted; 'or yield' at a yield sign is, by the words of the next sentence ('in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped'), a halt or slowing (drv.motion.slowing: forward motion with kin.accel_longitudinal below minus the resolution). kin.accel_longitudinal is not a stand-in for speed; both are read."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.stop_line", "st.entrance_of", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: st.stop_line recorded by st.entrance_of as marking x's approach carrier; nearness by st.region_geometry, side by prim.region_offset_along along the carrier's direction."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "st.entrance_of", "rel.occupies", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: the st.crosswalk st.entrance_of records as marking x's approach carrier, with the halt's footprint not overlapping it (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["st.intersection", "rel.occupies", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: footprint outside the intersection, distance by st.region_geometry."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s8", "standard": "a view of approaching traffic on the through highway: how much of the through highway must be in view", "concepts": ["st.sight_along_way", "st.highway", "st.on_way"], "params": ["p.intersection_sight_distance"], "convention": "Intersection sight distance for a stop- or yield-controlled approach (AASHTO Green Book cases B and C): from the place of the act, the through highway (a st.highway on which the intersection lies, st.on_way, and the subject's approach carrier does not) is in view for at least p.intersection_sight_distance (st.sight_along_way, the smaller of its two directions); not a stand-in for whether an actual road user is seen.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) through an approach carrier c it occupies (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c i); a dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governs c or i (dev.governs) at this observation; and traffic is not being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal: x being a member of traffic (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic), no dev.human_direction with role police_officer and no dev.traffic_signal that is not dev.inoperative governs c or i at this observation. Where x occupies several carriers entering i and the verdict differs between them, which governs is unknown.", "obligation": "Act: where a dev.stop_sign governs c or i, x halted (drv.motion.halted x with p.speed_resolution) at the place; where only a dev.yield_sign governs, x halted at the place or was slowing (drv.motion.slowing x with p.speed_resolution and p.deceleration_resolution) at some observation of the approach before passing the place (before the place is behind x along c by prim.region_offset_along; for place (3), before x enters i). Place, in the words' order: (1) where a stop line s (st.stop_line) is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of s c): at s, x's body within p.stop_point_tolerance of s (st_region_geometry_distance) and s not behind x along c (prim.region_offset_along x s c at least zero); (2) where the source observes that no stop line marks c and a crosswalk w is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of w c): before entering w, x's footprint not overlapping w, within p.stop_point_tolerance of w and w ahead along c; (3) where the source observes that neither marks c: x's footprint outside i, within p.stop_point_tolerance of i, or farther upstream where a highway h on which i lies and c does not (st.on_way i h; st.on_way c h false) is in view from x for at least p.intersection_sight_distance (st_sight_along_way x h). History bound (the approach convention): the search runs back from this entry to the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which x, on c, is outside the governing place's stopping zone upstream (not on it, short of it along c, farther than p.stop_point_tolerance), or to x's previous entry into i, whichever is later; the act found there meets the duty, reaching either end without it violates it, reaching neither leaves it unknown. An act before the previous entry into i never counts; an observed exit from the stopping zone upstream begins a new approach; crossing the mark, a change of carrier, a lateral move, a reverse within the zone and speed noise begin none. Missing evidence: whether this is an entry through c is unknown where the observation before it does not show x on a mapped carrier; a mark whose association with c is unobserved governs unknown; where the lists are observed and exclude c, the next place governs; a recorded act at a place known to govern decides compliance whatever else is missing.", "params": ["p.speed_resolution", "p.deceleration_resolution", "p.stop_point_tolerance", "p.intersection_sight_distance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'traffic is being controlled' is read as control of x's own approach or of the intersection it enters, x being a member of the traffic aggregate; the officer's role and the signal's presence are read as their official status.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'proper signs' are read through the presence of a stop or yield sign governing the approach or the intersection.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "At a yield sign the act owed at the place is read as the 'slowed or stopped' the next sentence names; yielding to traffic is the other node's duty.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'clearly marked' is read through the represented stop line.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "A halt within p.stop_point_tolerance of the intersection counts, and one farther upstream counts where the view bound holds; that no nearer point with the view existed is not checked.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "'the through highway' is read as a highway the intersection lies on that the subject's signed approach carrier does not lie on; its designation is presumed from the sign on the subject's approach.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "dev.stop_sign governs lane c (st.lane_enters c i); stop line s marks c; no officer and no signal. x is first observed 80 m upstream at 12 m/s, never falls to the speed resolution and enters i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x halts with its body 0.5 m short of s, then enters i."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "No sign governs c or i; x enters i without halting."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but dev.governs is not observed for the stop sign.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "dev.yield_sign governs c; x, moving forward at 10 m/s, decelerates at 2 m/s² 30 m upstream of s and enters i at 4 m/s without halting."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, but a dev.human_direction with role police_officer governs i while x rolls through."}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but the recording begins with x 1.5 m short of s at 1 m/s; no halt is recorded before x enters i.", "boundary": "x's approach start on c, the last observation outside the stopping zone upstream of s, lies before the recording."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.deceleration_resolution", "unit": "m/s^2", "value": 0.3, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest longitudinal deceleration the acquisition standard s