{"concept_id": "drv.motion.halted", "kind": "formula", "contract": "A road user is at a standstill at the observation. This is the corpus definition of a required stop, \"complete cessation from movement\", observed on sampled speeds: the road user's speed (kin.speed, m/s) is at or below speed_floor, the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as no movement. The state holds at each observation at which the speed is that low, with no minimum duration. Not denoted: where the road user stands, why it stands, or whether its engine runs or a brake is set.", "definition": "DEF-NRS-484A-255", "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "speed_floor", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "the source's speed resolution: a speed at or below it counts as no movement"}], "elements": [{"span": "the road user's speed (kin.speed, m/s) is at or below speed_floor", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.speed: 'magnitude of velocity' in m/s; the definition's absolute 'complete cessation from movement' is observed only within the resolution speed_floor names."}], "residues": [{"span": "when required", "why": "The definition's scope words ('when required') say which duties it serves; the caller is the duty that requires the stop, so the concept carries no condition for them."}], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x has kin.speed 0.0 m/s at the observation."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x has kin.speed 4.0 m/s at the observation."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "The source does not observe kin.speed for x.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_250_4_o1", "NRS_484B_250_4_o2", "NRS_484B_257_1_o1", "NRS_484B_270_3_o2"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.entering_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user x enters structure region r at the observation: its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before. The entry is that one observation; the later observations at which the overlap continues are not the entry again. Unknown where the overlap is unobserved at the observation or at the one before, or where there is no observation of x before it. Not denoted: x's direction or speed, the region x came from, or its whole body being inside r: an overlap by any part of the footprint counts.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [], "elements": [{"span": "its footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and did not at the observation before", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'; read at the observation and at the one before it, so the event is the observation at which the overlap became true."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x's footprint does not overlap r at t0 and overlaps r at t1; judged at t1."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x's footprint overlaps r at t0 and at t1; judged at t1, the overlap continues and is no entry."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "rel.occupies of x and r is not observed at t0; judged at t1.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_250_4_o1", "NRS_484B_250_4_o2", "NRS_484B_250_1", "NRS_484B_253_o2", "NRS_484B_257_1_o1", "NRS_484B_257_1_o2", "NRS_484B_263_o1", "NRS_484B_263_o2", "NRS_484B_270_3_o2", "NRS_484B_270_4"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.leaving_region", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user x leaves structure region r at the observation: its footprint overlapped r (rel.occupies) at the observation before and does not overlap it at the observation. The exit is that one observation; the later observations at which x stays off r are not the exit again. Unknown where the overlap is unobserved at the observation or at the one before, or where there is no observation of x before it. Not denoted: x's direction or speed, or the region x moves into.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}], "params": [], "elements": [{"span": "its footprint overlapped r (rel.occupies) at the observation before and does not overlap it at the observation", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'; its negation became true at the observation."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x's footprint overlaps r at t0 and does not at t1; judged at t1."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x's footprint overlaps r at t0 and at t1; judged at t1."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "rel.occupies of x and r is not observed at t1.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_263_o1", "NRS_484B_263_o2"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.position.entered_via", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user x is inside region r on its current entry and came in through region c: x's footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and at every observation since the observation at which this overlap began (the footprint overlapping r there and not at the observation before), and at that beginning x's footprint also overlapped c. Unknown where the beginning of the current overlap is not observed: an overlap already under way at x's first observation, or an unobserved overlap of r or c at an observation that decides it. Not denoted: that c is an approach to r (the caller states the entry topology), the direction x moved, or where x was before the beginning.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}, {"name": "r", "sort": "region"}, {"name": "c", "sort": "region"}], "params": [], "elements": [{"span": "x's footprint overlaps r (rel.occupies) at the observation and at every observation since the observation at which this overlap began", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies: 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'; held at every observation since its last rise (past mirror of until)."}, {"span": "at that beginning x's footprint also overlapped c", "atoms": ["rel.occupies"], "concepts": [], "justification": "rel.occupies of x and c read at the observation at which the overlap of r rose."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x overlaps c and not r at t0, overlaps c and r at t1, overlaps r only at t2; judged at t2."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x overlaps region c2 and not r at t0, overlaps c2 and r at t1 without overlapping c, overlaps r at t2; judged at t2."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "rel.occupies of x and c is not observed at t1, the observation at which x's overlap of r began; judged at t2.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_250_1", "NRS_484B_253_o1", "NRS_484B_253_o2", "NRS_484B_257_1_o2"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.road.opposed_directions", "kind": "formula", "contract": "The designated directions of two travel carriers point opposite ways: the dot product of their designated directions (st.lane_direction, read normalised, world frame) is below minus opposed_cosine, so the angle between them is wider than the angle whose cosine is minus opposed_cosine. Unknown where either carrier carries no designated direction. Not denoted: the motion or heading of any road user on them, the carriers lying on the same way, or their entering the same intersection: the caller states those.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "c1", "sort": "region"}, {"name": "c2", "sort": "region"}], "params": [{"name": "opposed_cosine", "unit": "ratio", "meaning": "minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between the two designated directions that counts as opposite"}], "elements": [{"span": "the dot product of their designated directions (st.lane_direction, read normalised, world frame) is below minus opposed_cosine", "atoms": ["st.lane_direction"], "concepts": [], "justification": "st.lane_direction: 'direction of travel designated for a structure a vehicle travels in'; read normalised, the product of the x components plus the product of the y components is the cosine of the angle between them."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "c1 has st.lane_direction (1, 0) and c2 (-1, 0)."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "c1 has st.lane_direction (1, 0) and c2 (0, 1): the carriers cross at a right angle."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "c2 carries no st.lane_direction in the source.", "masked": ["st.lane_direction"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_250_1", "NRS_484B_253_o1", "NRS_484B_253_o2"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.turning_left", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user x is turning to its left at the observation: it is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor) and its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive) exceeds yaw_floor, the source's yaw-rate resolution. It does not tell a turn at a junction from following a left-hand bend: the caller states the place. Not denoted: a completed turn manoeuvre, an intention to turn, or a turn indicator.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "speed_floor", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as no motion"}, {"name": "yaw_floor", "unit": "deg/s", "meaning": "the source's yaw-rate resolution, below which a reading counts as no heading change"}], "elements": [{"span": "it is moving (drv.motion.moving with speed_floor)", "atoms": ["kin.speed"], "concepts": ["drv.motion.moving"], "justification": "drv.motion.moving: 'its speed exceeds speed_floor'."}, {"span": "its yaw rate (kin.yaw_rate, deg/s, left positive) exceeds yaw_floor", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.yaw_rate: 'rate of change of heading, positive when the heading turns to the left'; not a stand-in for road curvature, which the contract does not claim to tell apart."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x has kin.speed 5 m/s and kin.yaw_rate 15 deg/s."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x has kin.speed 5 m/s and kin.yaw_rate -15 deg/s (turning right)."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "x has kin.speed 5 m/s and kin.yaw_rate is not observed.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_253_o1", "NRS_484B_253_o2"], "supersedes": null}
{"concept_id": "drv.motion.slowing", "kind": "formula", "contract": "Road user x is slowing while moving forward at the observation: the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along its heading (kin.heading, read normalised) exceeds speed_floor, and its longitudinal acceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal, m/s², signed along the heading) is below minus decel_floor, the source's acceleration resolution. Not denoted: slowing while backing, a brake lamp or a brake input, a halt, or how much the speed has fallen.", "definition": null, "args": [{"name": "x", "sort": "track"}], "params": [{"name": "speed_floor", "unit": "m/s", "meaning": "the source's speed resolution, below which a reading counts as no motion"}, {"name": "decel_floor", "unit": "m/s^2", "meaning": "the source's acceleration resolution, below which a deceleration counts as none"}], "elements": [{"span": "the component of its velocity (kin.velocity, m/s, world frame) along its heading (kin.heading, read normalised) exceeds speed_floor", "atoms": ["kin.velocity", "kin.heading"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.velocity: 'velocity vector'; kin.heading: 'direction the body points'; their product is forward motion, which excludes backing, where a negative acceleration along the heading speeds the body up."}, {"span": "its longitudinal acceleration (kin.accel_longitudinal, m/s², signed along the heading) is below minus decel_floor", "atoms": ["kin.accel_longitudinal"], "concepts": [], "justification": "kin.accel_longitudinal: 'acceleration along heading, signed'; not a stand-in for speed, which is read separately."}], "residues": [], "literals": [], "scenarios": [{"name": "holds", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x moves forward at 8 m/s along its heading with kin.accel_longitudinal -2.0 m/s²."}, {"name": "fails", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x moves forward at 8 m/s with kin.accel_longitudinal 0.0 m/s²."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "x moves forward at 8 m/s and kin.accel_longitudinal is not observed.", "masked": ["kin.accel_longitudinal"]}], "used_by": ["NRS_484B_257_1_o1"], "supersedes": null}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_250_4_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-250-4"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "When a vehicle enters an intersection", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "controlled by a traffic-control signal which is installed and has its vehicular signals uncovered, but is inoperative at the time the vehicle enters the intersection,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the driver of the vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall proceed as if a stop sign had been erected at each entrance to the intersection and shall stop at a clearly marked stop line or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection or, if there is none, at the point nearest the intersection", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "After making such a stop,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "the driver shall proceed", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "cautiously,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "yielding to vehicles", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s13", "text": "which have previously completed a stop", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s14", "text": "or are within the intersection.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle. 'enters an intersection' is drv.motion.entering_region on a region of kind st.intersection ('the region where two roadways meet'; DEF-NRS-484A-105 'the area embraced within the prolongation ... of the lateral curb lines'; the alley junction its (3) excludes is excluded by the atom's own contract), read through rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'. st.intersection is not a stand-in for a crosswalk or stop line: the entry is into the junction itself."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.traffic_signal", "dev.inoperative", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "dev.traffic_signal 'a signal head' is the traffic-control signal (DEF-NRS-484A-290 'by which traffic is alternately directed to stop or proceed'); dev.inoperative 'a signal head installed and uncovered but showing no valid indication' carries 'installed and has its vehicular signals uncovered, but is inoperative' word for word. 'controlled by' is dev.governs 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection': the signal governs the intersection or the approach carrier (st.lane_enters 'the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into', a carrier of kind st.travel_region the subject occupies); dev.governs is not a stand-in for a position and none is read from it. 'at the time the vehicle enters' fixes the reading to the entry observation."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the driver of the vehicle': the duty binds the vehicle's controlled motion (DEF-NRS-484A-080 'every person who drives or is in actual physical control of a vehicle'), read through the vehicle of the admitted aggregate; who controls it is not observable."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["kin.speed", "st.stop_line", "st.entrance_of", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along", "st.crosswalk", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.halted"], "justification": "'shall stop' is a required stop, DEF-NRS-484A-255 'complete cessation from movement', carried by drv.motion.halted over kin.speed 'magnitude of velocity'. 'proceed as if a stop sign had been erected at each entrance' states the halt a stop sign requires (dev.stop_sign 'regulatory sign requiring a full halt') together with the yield of the next sentence; no sign is erected, so no device is read: the halt carries it here and the yield is the other node's. 'at a clearly marked stop line': st.stop_line 'the transverse line marking where vehicles halt', tied to the subject's approach by st.entrance_of 'the carrier whose entrance into an intersection a stop line or a crosswalk marks', read on the same carrier (of kind st.travel_region) as st.lane_enters (distance never stands for belonging); nearness by st.region_geometry 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it' (not a stand-in for occupancy, which is not read from it), side by prim.region_offset_along 'measured along a carrier's designated direction'. 'before entering the crosswalk on the near side': st.crosswalk 'marked crossing, or the unmarked prolongation of sidewalks at an intersection' (DEF-NRS-484A-065 both parts) that st.entrance_of records as marking the approach carrier, with rel.occupies of it false at the halt; st.crosswalk is not a stand-in for a stop line. 'at the point nearest the intersection': a halt with the footprint outside the st.intersection (rel.occupies false), its distance read by st.region_geometry; st.intersection is not a stand-in for the crosswalk or stop line absent on this branch."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s8", "standard": "a view of approaching traffic on the through highway: how much of the crossing way must be in view", "concepts": ["st.sight_along_way", "st.highway", "st.on_way"], "params": ["p.intersection_sight_distance"], "convention": "Intersection sight distance for a stop-controlled approach (AASHTO Green Book case B): from the halt, the crossing way (a st.highway on which the intersection lies, st.on_way, and the approach carrier does not) is in view for at least p.intersection_sight_distance in the smaller of its two directions (st.sight_along_way 'the distance along a way ... within which another vehicle on that way could be seen from the road user's eye ... the smaller of the two directions'). st.sight_along_way is not a stand-in for whether an actual road user is seen: the view of approaching traffic is the view along the way whether or not traffic is present.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters an intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) through an approach carrier c: a region of kind st.travel_region that x occupies at this observation with st.lane_enters c i. At this observation some traffic signal d (dev.traffic_signal) that governs i or c (dev.governs d i, or dev.governs d c) is inoperative (dev.inoperative d). Where x occupies several carriers entering i and the verdict differs between them, which governs is unknown; a rule never picks the carrier that favours x.", "obligation": "Act: x halted (drv.motion.halted x with p.speed_resolution) at the place the words name, taken in their order, on the approach that leads to this entry. Place: (1) where a stop line s (st.stop_line) is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of s c): at s, an observation at which x is halted, its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of s (st_region_geometry_distance x s) and s not behind x along c's designated direction (prim.region_offset_along x s c at least zero); (2) where the source observes the stop lines' entrances and none marks c, and a crosswalk w is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of w c): before entering w, an observation at which x is halted, its footprint not overlapping w (rel.occupies x w false), its body within p.stop_point_tolerance of w and w ahead of x along c (prim.region_offset_along x w c positive); (3) where the source observes that no stop line and no crosswalk marks c: an observation at which x is halted with its footprint outside i (rel.occupies x i false), within p.stop_point_tolerance of i, or farther upstream where a highway h on which i lies and c does not (st.on_way i h; st.on_way c h false) is in view from x for at least p.intersection_sight_distance (st_sight_along_way x h). History bound (the ontology's approach convention): the search runs back from this entry and ends at the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which x, on c, is outside the governing place's stopping zone upstream (not on the place, short of it along c by prim.region_offset_along, and farther from it than p.stop_point_tolerance by st_region_geometry_distance; for place (3) the place is c's entrance end at i), or at x's previous entry into i, whichever is later. A halt found in that stretch meets the duty; reaching either end without one violates it; reaching neither (the recording begins inside the approach) leaves it unknown. A halt before the previous entry into i never counts for this entry. An observed exit from the stopping zone upstream begins a new approach and the halt is owed again; crossing the mark, moving on, a change of carrier or a lateral move within this entry, a reverse that stays within the zone and speed noise begin none. Missing evidence: whether this is an entry through c is unknown where the observation before it does not show x on a mapped carrier; where a stop line's or crosswalk's association with c is unobserved, whether it governs is unknown; where the association lists are observed and exclude c, the next place in the words' order governs and the duty is not unknown on that ground; a recorded halt at a place known to govern decides compliance whatever else is missing.", "params": ["p.speed_resolution", "p.stop_point_tolerance", "p.intersection_sight_distance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "'traffic-control signal' is an official device (DEF-NRS-484A-290 'placed or erected by a public authority or railroad'); the signal head's presence on the road is read as that status.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion, whoever or whatever controls it.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "'clearly marked' is read through the represented stop line; paint clarity is not modelled, and which place governs, the halt and its timing are unchanged.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "'the point nearest the intersection where the driver has a view': a halt within p.stop_point_tolerance of the intersection counts, and a halt farther upstream counts where the view bound holds there; that no nearer point with the view existed is not checked, since no atom compares points along the approach for their view.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "'the through highway' at an intersection whose signal is dark is read as a highway the intersection lies on that the subject's approach carrier does not lie on (st.on_way): every entrance is treated as stop-controlled, so the crossing way is the one whose traffic the driver must see; its designation as a through highway is a status no feature shows here.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x (motor vehicle class, member of the vehicle aggregate) drives on lane c with st.lane_enters c i; stop line s with st.entrance_of s c; dev.traffic_signal d governs i and is dev.inoperative. x is first observed 80 m upstream of s at 12 m/s, keeps kin.speed above 3 m/s past s and enters i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x halts (kin.speed 0) with its body 0.5 m short of s, s ahead along c, then moves on and enters i."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, but d shows circular_green and dev.inoperative is false at x's entry into i."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but the source does not observe dev.inoperative for d.", "masked": ["dev.inoperative"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "No stop line marks c (the line list is observed); crosswalk w with st.entrance_of w c; d inoperative. x halts with its footprint overlapping w, then enters i: the halt is not before entering the crosswalk and no other halt occurs on the approach."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "No stop line and no crosswalk marks c; d inoperative. x halts outside i, 1 m from it, then enters i."}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but the recording begins with x already on c 1.5 m short of s at 1 m/s, inside the stopping zone; no halt is recorded before x enters i.", "boundary": "x's approach start on c, the last observation outside the stopping zone upstream of s, lies before the recording."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.stop_point_tolerance", "unit": "m", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Stop-point tolerance: the largest ground distance between a halted body and the line, crossing or intersection edge at which the halt counts as made at that place; a body farther upstream is outside the stopping zone.", "source": "MUTCD 2009 section 3B.16 stop-line placement (at least 4 ft ahead of the crosswalk) and vehicle positioning variability at a stop"}, {"name": "p.intersection_sight_distance", "unit": "m", "value": 100, "convention": "Intersection sight distance: the length of the crossing way, in the smaller of its two directions, that a driver halted on a stop-controlled approach must be able to see to judge a gap in approaching traffic.", "source": "AASHTO A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets (2018) section 9.5.3, case B departure sight triangles at a low urban design speed"}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_250_4_o2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-250-4"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "When a vehicle enters an intersection", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "controlled by a traffic-control signal which is installed and has its vehicular signals uncovered, but is inoperative at the time the vehicle enters the intersection,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the driver of the vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall proceed as if a stop sign had been erected at each entrance to the intersection and shall stop", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "at a clearly marked stop line", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "or, if there is none, at the point nearest the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "After making such a stop,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "the driver shall proceed", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "cautiously,", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "yielding to vehicles", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s13", "text": "which have previously completed a stop", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s14", "text": "or are within the intersection.", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: 'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'enters an intersection' is drv.motion.entering_region on a st.intersection ('the region where two roadways meet') through rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.traffic_signal", "dev.inoperative", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: dev.inoperative 'a signal head installed and uncovered but showing no valid indication' of a dev.traffic_signal that governs ('the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection') the intersection or the approach carrier (st.lane_enters) x occupies, read at the entry."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the driver of the vehicle' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (DEF-NRS-484A-080)."}, {"span": "s10", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'shall proceed' after the stop is the subject's entry into the intersection (drv.motion.entering_region, rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region'): the observation at which it proceeds in preference to others or not."}, {"span": "s12", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'yielding to vehicles' (DEF-NRS-484A-210 right-of-way 'the right ... to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle'): x does not enter the intersection while a vehicle of the admitted aggregate is owed precedence; the yield is read at x's entry."}, {"span": "s13", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.intersection", "kin.speed"], "derived": ["drv.motion.halted"], "justification": "'which have previously completed a stop': another vehicle y halted (drv.motion.halted, DEF-NRS-484A-255 'complete cessation from movement') on another approach carrier of the intersection (st.lane_enters 'the intersection region a directed approach carrier runs into', rel.occupies) before x's own halt began, and has stayed on that carrier outside the intersection since."}, {"span": "s14", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'are within the intersection': rel.occupies of y and the intersection x enters, at x's entry."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s11", "standard": "proceed cautiously", "concepts": ["prim.closest_approach_within", "prim.closest_approach_distance"], "params": ["p.immediate_hazard_gap", "p.conflict_clearance"], "convention": "Surrogate safety measure of a conflict (FHWA SSAM): at x's entry, no other road user's centre is predicted, under constant velocities, to come within p.conflict_clearance of x's within p.immediate_hazard_gap. The primitives are not a stand-in for contact or the danger of a crash by themselves; the bound the parameters set is the standard's.", "surrogate": true}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "s9", "rule": "NRS_484B_250_4_o1", "map": {"x": "x"}, "as": "compliance"}], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) through an approach carrier c (st.travel_region, x occupies c, st.lane_enters c i); a traffic signal (dev.traffic_signal) that governs i or c (dev.governs) is dev.inoperative at this observation; and NRS_484B_250_4_o1 is complied with for x at this observation (rule NRS_484B_250_4_o1 {x -> x}). That rule is engaged at exactly this entry, so its compliance here is the fact 'such a stop' refers to: x halted, on the approach to this entry, at the place it requires.", "obligation": "At this entry: (1) no vehicle y other than x (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) occupies i (rel.occupies y i); (2) no vehicle y other than x waits on another approach carrier c2 of i (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c2 i, x not on c2) having completed a stop before x: y has occupied c2 and not i at every observation since an observation at which x's halt on c began (x halted, drv.motion.halted with p.speed_resolution, and on c there, and not halted at the observation before) and y was already halted on c2 (halted there and at the observation before); (3) proceeding cautiously: no road user z other than x is in predicted conflict with x, i.e. not both prim.closest_approach_within x z with horizon p.immediate_hazard_gap and prim.closest_approach_distance x z with the same horizon below p.conflict_clearance.", "params": ["p.speed_resolution", "p.immediate_hazard_gap", "p.conflict_clearance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s2", "why": "The signal head's presence is read as the official status of the traffic-control signal.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s11", "why": "'cautiously' names no factor; it is read only through the predicted conflict at the entry, and marked surrogate as a standard of care.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s12", "why": "The yield is judged at x's entry into the intersection: an entry while a vehicle is owed precedence is the failure to yield; conduct after the entry is not read for this yield.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Signal d governing i is dev.inoperative; x halts within 0.5 m of the stop line marking its lane c, then enters i while vehicle y occupies i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x is the only road user in the scene when it enters i after its halt."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "Signal d shows circular_green (not dev.inoperative) when x enters i."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but rel.occupies of y and i is not observed at x's entry.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x halts at its stop line; vehicle y had halted at the stop line of crossing carrier c2 two seconds before x's halt began and still waits there, outside i; x enters i first."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, but x halted 30 m upstream of the stop line marking c (outside the stopping zone) and rolled through the line: the halt was not such a stop, NRS_484B_250_4_o1 is not complied with, and this duty does not arise."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.immediate_hazard_gap", "unit": "s", "value": 4.1, "convention": "Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.", "source": "HCM 7th ed. Exhibit 20-11 base critical headway (major-street left turn)"}, {"name": "p.conflict_clearance", "unit": "m", "value": 3.0, "convention": "Conflict radius: the centre distance at predicted closest approach below which two road users' paths count as in conflict; about the half-length plus half-width of two passenger cars.", "source": "FHWA Surrogate Safety Assessment Model (Gettman et al. 2008) conflict definition"}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_250_1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-250-1"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "approaching an intersection", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "to a vehicle which has entered the intersection from a different highway.", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "Except as otherwise provided in subsection 4 [NRS-484B-250-4],", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "this section does not apply at intersections controlled by official traffic-control devices", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "or to vehicles approaching each other from opposite directions,", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "when the driver of one of the vehicles is intending to", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "or is making a left turn.", "role": "exception"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is admitted as DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion (DEF-NRS-484A-080)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'approaching an intersection': x occupies (rel.occupies) a carrier of kind st.travel_region whose entrance end is the intersection (st.lane_enters 'the carrier is an approach to that intersection'); the yield is decided at the observation at which x enters it (drv.motion.entering_region), where x still occupies that approach carrier. st.lane_enters is not a stand-in for the subject's presence in the intersection, which rel.occupies reads."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'yield the right-of-way' (DEF-NRS-484A-210 'the right ... to proceed in a lawful manner in preference to another vehicle'): x does not enter the intersection (drv.motion.entering_region over rel.occupies) while a vehicle owed precedence is in it."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": ["drv.position.entered_via"], "justification": "'a vehicle' is the admitted aggregate. 'which has entered the intersection' is rel.occupies of y and the intersection on y's current entry, and 'from a different highway' is the carrier y entered through (drv.position.entered_via, st.lane_enters) lying on a st.highway ('the entire public way between its boundary lines') through st.on_way ('the public way ... a structure region lies on') on which x's approach carrier does not lie. The intersection lies on every way that meets there, so the way is read from the carriers, never the intersection."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["dev.traffic_signal", "dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'official traffic-control devices' (DEF-NRS-484A-145 'every sign, signal, marking and device ... for the purpose of regulating, warning or guiding traffic') that control the intersection: a dev.traffic_signal, dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt') or dev.yield_sign ('regulatory sign requiring yielding') governing the intersection or x's approach carrier (dev.governs 'the travel regions whose traffic the device controls ... or an intersection'). dev.governs is not a stand-in for a position."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.road.opposed_directions", "drv.position.entered_via"], "justification": "'approaching each other from opposite directions': read, as rel.oncoming's contract directs, through the carriers they approach through: x's approach carrier and the carrier y entered through (drv.position.entered_via) have opposed designated directions (drv.road.opposed_directions over st.lane_direction). rel.oncoming is not used: a turn makes current headings cease to be opposed while the approach direction is unchanged."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"], "justification": "'is making a left turn': the vehicle's heading change since it entered the intersection (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry, left positive, integrated from kin.yaw_rate) is at least the turn recognition angle; a bend of the way inside the region also changes it, which a right-angled junction does not offer."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "s8", "id": "int.left_turn", "meaning": "The source's current plan for the road user includes a left turn at the target region."}], "compositions": [{"span": "s5", "rule": "NRS_484B_250_4_o1", "map": {"x": "x"}, "as": "unless", "scopes": "s6"}], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) from an approach carrier c it occupies (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c i). Device exception (s6): the duty does not apply where some dev.traffic_signal, dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governs i or c (dev.governs) at this observation; this exception is suspended where NRS_484B_250_4_o1 applies to x here (ruleApplies NRS_484B_250_4_o1 {x -> x}: an entry under an inoperative signal).", "obligation": "At this entry no vehicle y other than x (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) occupies i having entered it from a different highway: y occupies i, entered it through a carrier c2 (drv.position.entered_via y i c2, st.lane_enters c2 i) that lies on a highway h2 (st.highway, st.on_way c2 h2) on which c does not lie (st.on_way c h2 false). Pair exception (s7 to s9): a y is excluded where c and c2 have opposed designated directions (drv.road.opposed_directions c c2 with p.opposed_carriers_cosine) and x or y intends a left turn at i (intent int.left_turn x i, or intent int.left_turn y i) or is making one (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry of x or of y and i, with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph, at least p.turn_recognition_angle).", "params": ["p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_recognition_angle"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "The yield is judged at x's entry into the intersection: an entry while a vehicle from a different highway is in it is the failure to yield.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s6", "why": "'official' is read through the device's presence; the devices that control an intersection are read as traffic signals, stop signs and yield signs governing the intersection or the subject's approach (a marking or a warning sign alone controls no right-of-way there).", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "No device governs i or its approaches. Vehicle y entered i from carrier c2 on highway h2; x, on carrier c on highway h (c not on h2), enters i while y occupies i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x waits on c until y has left i and enters i as the only road user in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "A dev.stop_sign governs c; signals are absent; x enters i while y occupies i."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but rel.occupies of y and i is not observed at x's entry.", "masked": ["rel.occupies"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "A dev.traffic_signal governing i is dev.inoperative (NRS_484B_250_4_o1 applies); y entered i from a different highway; x enters i while y occupies it."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "At a skewed junction, y entered i through c2 on another highway whose designated direction is opposed to c's, and int.left_turn y i is declared; x enters while y is in i: the pair is excepted."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.7, "convention": "Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.", "source": "Junction geometry: approaches meeting at an intersection skewed by up to 45 degrees (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9)"}, {"name": "p.turn_recognition_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 45, "convention": "Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.", "source": "Geometry of a right-angled junction (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9 intersection angles)"}], "gaps": []}
