: ["kin.yaw_rate", "kin.speed"], "derived": ["drv.motion.turning_left"], "justification": "'shall yield the right-of-way' (DEF-NRS-484A-210 'the right ... to proceed ... in preference'): a driver already within the intersection proceeds in preference by making its left turn; yielding is not turning left (drv.motion.turning_left: moving with kin.yaw_rate, left positive, above the resolution) while a vehicle owed precedence is present."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": ["drv.road.opposed_directions", "drv.position.entered_via"], "justification": "'any vehicle' is the admitted aggregate. 'approaching from the opposite direction' is read, as rel.oncoming's 'not a stand-in' clause directs, through the carriers: y's approach carrier of the intersection (one it occupies, or the one it entered through) has a designated direction opposed to that of x's approach carrier (drv.road.opposed_directions)."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'which is within the intersection': rel.occupies of y and the intersection x is in."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s7", "standard": "so close to the intersection as to constitute an immediate hazard", "concepts": ["st.region_geometry", "kin.speed"], "params": ["p.immediate_hazard_gap"], "convention": "Gap acceptance (HCM critical headway): an approaching vehicle outside the intersection is an immediate hazard where its ground distance to the intersection (st.region_geometry 'the ground distance from a road user's body outline to it') is at most its speed (kin.speed) times p.immediate_hazard_gap, so the bound moves with both proximity and speed.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "s3", "id": "int.left_turn", "meaning": "The source's current plan for the road user includes a left turn at the target region."}], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "b