i until y has passed, then turns left (kin.yaw_rate 15 deg/s, 4 m/s) as the only road user in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "x occupies i and the source declares int.left_turn x i false (x goes straight)."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but kin.yaw_rate of x is not observed.", "masked": ["kin.yaw_rate"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "Vehicle y occupies i, having entered through c2 opposed to c; x turns left (moving, kin.yaw_rate 12 deg/s)."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "Vehicle y on c2 opposed to c is 200 m from i at 15 m/s; x turns left."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.yaw_rate_resolution", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest yaw rate the acquisition standard separates from a straight path; a yaw rate at or below it counts as no heading change.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: yaw-rate resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.7, "convention": "Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.", "source": "Junction geometry: approaches meeting at an intersection skewed by up to 45 degrees (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9)"}, {"name": "p.immediate_hazard_gap", "unit": "s", "value": 4.1, "convention": "Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.", "source": "HCM 7th ed. Exhibit 20-11 base critical headway (major-street left turn)"}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_253_o2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-253"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "The driver of a vehicle", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "within an intersection", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "intending to turn to the left", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "to any vehicle approaching from the opposite direction", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "which is within the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "or so close thereto as to constitute an immediate hazard,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "but such driver, having so yielded", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "and having given a signal", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "when and as required,", "role": "reference"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "may make such left turn", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "and the drivers of all other vehicles", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s13", "text": "approaching the intersection from the opposite direction", "role": "trigger"}, {"id": "s14", "text": "shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s15", "text": "to the vehicle making the left turn.", "role": "condition"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "The turning vehicle y is of the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'the driver' is read through its controlled motion."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'within an intersection': rel.occupies 'a road user's footprint overlaps a lane / region' of y and the st.intersection x approaches."}, {"span": "s9", "atoms": ["sig.turn_indicator", "sig.hand_signal", "rel.occupies", "st.travel_region", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.position.entered_via"], "justification": "'having given a signal': sig.turn_indicator state left ('the signal that precedes a manoeuvre') or sig.hand_signal meaning left ('a driver's or rider's arm signal'), at some observation of y's continuous presence on its approach carrier (the one it entered through, drv.position.entered_via) or in the intersection up to now. Neither is a stand-in for the turn itself, which s11 reads."}, {"span": "s11", "atoms": ["kin.yaw_rate", "kin.speed", "rel.occupies"], "derived": ["drv.motion.turning_left", "drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry"], "justification": "'may make such left turn': y is making it, turning left now (drv.motion.turning_left: moving, kin.yaw_rate left positive above resolution) or having turned left since entering the intersection by at least the turn recognition angle (drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry)."}, {"span": "s12", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the drivers of all other vehicles': x, any vehicle of the admitted aggregate other than the turning one, read through its controlled motion."}, {"span": "s13", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region", "drv.road.opposed_directions", "drv.position.entered_via"], "justification": "'approaching the intersection': x occupies an approach carrier c (st.lane_enters) and its yield is decided at its entry (drv.motion.entering_region). 'from the opposite direction' relative to the turning vehicle: c and the carrier y entered through (drv.position.entered_via) have opposed designated directions (drv.road.opposed_directions), as rel.oncoming's 'not a stand-in' clause directs."}, {"span": "s14", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'shall yield the right-of-way' (DEF-NRS-484A-210): x does not enter the intersection while the turning vehicle is owed precedence."}, {"span": "s15", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": [], "justification": "'the vehicle making the left turn': the vehicle y (admitted aggregate) in the intersection that s11 reads as making the turn."}], "operationalizations": [], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [{"span": "s3", "id": "int.left_turn", "meaning": "The source's current plan for the road user includes a left turn at the target region."}], "compositions": [{"span": "s8", "rule": "NRS_484B_253_o1", "map": {"x": "y"}, "as": "compliance"}], "residues": [{"span": "s10", "why": "'when and as required' refers to the signalling requirements of a law outside this corpus (no bracketed id resolves it); the signal itself is read on s9."}], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) from an approach carrier c it occupies (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c i).", "obligation": "At this entry no vehicle y other than x (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) is making a left turn in i under the words' conditions: y occupies i, having entered it through a carrier c2 (drv.position.entered_via y i c2, st.lane_enters c2 i) with drv.road.opposed_directions c c2 (p.opposed_carriers_cosine); the source declares int.left_turn y i; y is making the turn (drv.motion.turning_left y with p.speed_resolution and p.yaw_rate_resolution, or drv.motion.heading_change_since_entry y i with step p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph at least p.turn_recognition_angle); y has so yielded (rule NRS_484B_253_o1 {x -> y} complied with at every observation since y's current overlap of i began); and y has given a signal (sig.turn_indicator left, or sig.hand_signal left) at some observation since y last came onto c2 while it has stayed on c2 or in i since.", "params": ["p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "p.speed_resolution", "p.yaw_rate_resolution", "p.heading_since_step_carla_scene_graph", "p.turn_recognition_angle"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'the driver' of the turning vehicle is read through its controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s12", "why": "'the drivers' are read through the vehicles' controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s14", "why": "The yield is judged at x's entry into the intersection while the turning vehicle is in it.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "y entered i through c2 with sig.turn_indicator left on c2, int.left_turn y i declared, waited in i while no opposing vehicle was near, and now turns left (kin.yaw_rate 15 deg/s, 4 m/s); x on c (opposed to c2) enters i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "x waits on c and enters i after y has left it, as the only road user in i."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "x drives along a road segment and enters no intersection."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but neither sig.turn_indicator nor sig.hand_signal of y is observed.", "masked": ["sig.turn_indicator", "sig.hand_signal"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but y's sig.turn_indicator is off and sig.hand_signal no_signal at every observation: y gave no signal, and x owes it no precedence under this duty."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but y began its turn while x was 15 m from i at 15 m/s on c, so NRS_484B_253_o1 was not complied with by y: y has not so yielded."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.opposed_carriers_cosine", "unit": "ratio", "value": 0.7, "convention": "Direction tolerance: minus the cosine of the narrowest angle between two carriers' designated directions that counts as opposite directions; carriers within about 45 degrees of exactly opposed count.", "source": "Junction geometry: approaches meeting at an intersection skewed by up to 45 degrees (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9)"}, {"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.yaw_rate_resolution", "unit": "deg/s", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest yaw rate the acquisition standard separates from a straight path; a yaw rate at or below it counts as no heading change.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: yaw-rate resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.turn_recognition_angle", "unit": "deg", "value": 45, "convention": "Turn recognition: the heading change through an intersection beyond which a passage counts as a turn rather than a straight crossing; half the right angle of a turn at a right-angled junction, leaving room for skewed junctions and lane offsets.", "source": "Geometry of a right-angled junction (AASHTO Green Book ch. 9 intersection angles)"}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_257_1_o1", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-257-1"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "When proper signs have been erected,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall stop or yield at a clearly marked stop line or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection or, if there is none, then at the point nearest the intersection", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.", "role": "standard"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "After having stopped or, in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped,", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "the driver shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "to other vehicles which have entered the intersection from such through highway", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "or which are approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.", "role": "sibling"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "dev.human_direction", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.inoperative", "dev.governs", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "'traffic' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic; the traffic whose control matters is the subject's own flow, so x is read as a member. 'being controlled by a police officer' is dev.human_direction 'a person directing traffic' with role police_officer (DEF-NRS-484A-180 'every officer authorized to direct or regulate traffic') governing the intersection or x's approach carrier (dev.governs); 'or a traffic-control signal' is a dev.traffic_signal governing them that is not dev.inoperative ('showing no valid indication'): a dark signal controls nothing, and NRS 484B.250(4) then governs."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'proper signs' are dev.stop_sign ('regulatory sign requiring a full halt') or dev.yield_sign ('regulatory sign requiring yielding without a mandatory halt') governing (dev.governs) x's approach carrier c (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters c i) or the intersection; the duty is owed on the approach to x's entry into the intersection (drv.motion.entering_region)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle; 'the driver' is read through its controlled motion."}, {"span": "s4", "atoms": ["kin.speed", "kin.velocity", "kin.heading", "kin.accel_longitudinal"], "derived": ["drv.motion.halted", "drv.motion.slowing"], "justification": "'stop' (required: DEF-NRS-484A-255 'complete cessation from movement') is drv.motion.halted; 'or yield' at a yield sign is, by the words of the next sentence ('in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped'), a halt or slowing (drv.motion.slowing: forward motion with kin.accel_longitudinal below minus the resolution). kin.accel_longitudinal is not a stand-in for speed; both are read."}, {"span": "s5", "atoms": ["st.stop_line", "st.entrance_of", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: st.stop_line recorded by st.entrance_of as marking x's approach carrier; nearness by st.region_geometry, side by prim.region_offset_along along the carrier's direction."}, {"span": "s6", "atoms": ["st.crosswalk", "st.entrance_of", "rel.occupies", "st.region_geometry", "prim.region_offset_along"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: the st.crosswalk st.entrance_of records as marking x's approach carrier, with the halt's footprint not overlapping it (rel.occupies)."}, {"span": "s7", "atoms": ["st.intersection", "rel.occupies", "st.region_geometry"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_250_4_o1: footprint outside the intersection, distance by st.region_geometry."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s8", "standard": "a view of approaching traffic on the through highway: how much of the through highway must be in view", "concepts": ["st.sight_along_way", "st.highway", "st.on_way"], "params": ["p.intersection_sight_distance"], "convention": "Intersection sight distance for a stop- or yield-controlled approach (AASHTO Green Book cases B and C): from the place of the act, the through highway (a st.highway on which the intersection lies, st.on_way, and the subject's approach carrier does not) is in view for at least p.intersection_sight_distance (st.sight_along_way, the smaller of its two directions); not a stand-in for whether an actual road user is seen.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "x is a vehicle (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) and enters intersection i (st.intersection) at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) through an approach carrier c it occupies (st.travel_region, st.lane_enters c i); a dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governs c or i (dev.governs) at this observation; and traffic is not being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal: x being a member of traffic (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic), no dev.human_direction with role police_officer and no dev.traffic_signal that is not dev.inoperative governs c or i at this observation. Where x occupies several carriers entering i and the verdict differs between them, which governs is unknown.", "obligation": "Act: where a dev.stop_sign governs c or i, x halted (drv.motion.halted x with p.speed_resolution) at the place; where only a dev.yield_sign governs, x halted at the place or was slowing (drv.motion.slowing x with p.speed_resolution and p.deceleration_resolution) at some observation of the approach before passing the place (before the place is behind x along c by prim.region_offset_along; for place (3), before x enters i). Place, in the words' order: (1) where a stop line s (st.stop_line) is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of s c): at s, x's body within p.stop_point_tolerance of s (st_region_geometry_distance) and s not behind x along c (prim.region_offset_along x s c at least zero); (2) where the source observes that no stop line marks c and a crosswalk w is recorded as marking c (st.entrance_of w c): before entering w, x's footprint not overlapping w, within p.stop_point_tolerance of w and w ahead along c; (3) where the source observes that neither marks c: x's footprint outside i, within p.stop_point_tolerance of i, or farther upstream where a highway h on which i lies and c does not (st.on_way i h; st.on_way c h false) is in view from x for at least p.intersection_sight_distance (st_sight_along_way x h). History bound (the approach convention): the search runs back from this entry to the approach start, the last observation before the entry at which x, on c, is outside the governing place's stopping zone upstream (not on it, short of it along c, farther than p.stop_point_tolerance), or to x's previous entry into i, whichever is later; the act found there meets the duty, reaching either end without it violates it, reaching neither leaves it unknown. An act before the previous entry into i never counts; an observed exit from the stopping zone upstream begins a new approach; crossing the mark, a change of carrier, a lateral move, a reverse within the zone and speed noise begin none. Missing evidence: whether this is an entry through c is unknown where the observation before it does not show x on a mapped carrier; a mark whose association with c is unobserved governs unknown; where the lists are observed and exclude c, the next place governs; a recorded act at a place known to govern decides compliance whatever else is missing.", "params": ["p.speed_resolution", "p.deceleration_resolution", "p.stop_point_tolerance", "p.intersection_sight_distance"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "'traffic is being controlled' is read as control of x's own approach or of the intersection it enters, x being a member of the traffic aggregate; the officer's role and the signal's presence are read as their official status.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'proper signs' are read through the presence of a stop or yield sign governing the approach or the intersection.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s4", "why": "At a yield sign the act owed at the place is read as the 'slowed or stopped' the next sentence names; yielding to traffic is the other node's duty.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s5", "why": "'clearly marked' is read through the represented stop line.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s7", "why": "A halt within p.stop_point_tolerance of the intersection counts, and one farther upstream counts where the view bound holds; that no nearer point with the view existed is not checked.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s8", "why": "'the through highway' is read as a highway the intersection lies on that the subject's signed approach carrier does not lie on; its designation is presumed from the sign on the subject's approach.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "dev.stop_sign governs lane c (st.lane_enters c i); stop line s marks c; no officer and no signal. x is first observed 80 m upstream at 12 m/s, never falls to the speed resolution and enters i."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x halts with its body 0.5 m short of s, then enters i."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "No sign governs c or i; x enters i without halting."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but dev.governs is not observed for the stop sign.", "masked": ["dev.governs"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "dev.yield_sign governs c; x, moving forward at 10 m/s, decelerates at 2 m/s² 30 m upstream of s and enters i at 4 m/s without halting."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, but a dev.human_direction with role police_officer governs i while x rolls through."}, {"name": "history_boundary", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but the recording begins with x 1.5 m short of s at 1 m/s; no halt is recorded before x enters i.", "boundary": "x's approach start on c, the last observation outside the stopping zone upstream of s, lies before the recording."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.speed_resolution", "unit": "m/s", "value": 0.2, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest speed the acquisition standard separates from standstill; a speed at or below it counts as no motion.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: speed resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.deceleration_resolution", "unit": "m/s^2", "value": 0.3, "convention": "Sensor resolution: the smallest longitudinal deceleration the acquisition standard separates from steady speed; a deceleration at or below it counts as no slowing.", "source": "carla_scene_graph acquisition standard: acceleration resolution of the recorded kinematics"}, {"name": "p.stop_point_tolerance", "unit": "m", "value": 2.0, "convention": "Stop-point tolerance: the largest ground distance between a halted body and the line, crossing or intersection edge at which the halt counts as made at that place; a body farther upstream is outside the stopping zone.", "source": "MUTCD 2009 section 3B.16 stop-line placement (at least 4 ft ahead of the crosswalk) and vehicle positioning variability at a stop"}, {"name": "p.intersection_sight_distance", "unit": "m", "value": 100, "convention": "Intersection sight distance: the length of the crossing way, in the smaller of its two directions, that a driver halted on a stop-controlled approach must be able to see to judge a gap in approaching traffic.", "source": "AASHTO A Policy on Geometric Design of Highways and Streets (2018) section 9.5.3, case B departure sight triangles at a low urban design speed"}], "gaps": []}
{"node_id": "NRS_484B_257_1_o2", "law_refs": ["NRS-484B-257-1"], "subject": {"binder": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}, "segmentation": [{"id": "s1", "text": "Except when traffic is being controlled by a police officer or a traffic-control signal:", "role": "exception"}, {"id": "s2", "text": "When proper signs have been erected,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s3", "text": "the driver of a vehicle", "role": "subject"}, {"id": "s4", "text": "shall stop or yield", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s5", "text": "at a clearly marked stop line", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s6", "text": "or, if there is none, before entering the crosswalk on the near side of the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s7", "text": "or, if there is none, then at the point nearest the intersection", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s8", "text": "where the driver has a view of approaching traffic on the through highway.", "role": "sibling"}, {"id": "s9", "text": "After having stopped or, in the event of a yield sign, slowed or stopped,", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s10", "text": "the driver shall yield the right-of-way", "role": "obligation"}, {"id": "s11", "text": "to other vehicles which have entered the intersection from such through highway", "role": "condition"}, {"id": "s12", "text": "or which are approaching so closely on such through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection.", "role": "standard"}], "elements": [{"span": "s1", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic", "dev.human_direction", "dev.traffic_signal", "dev.inoperative", "dev.governs", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region"], "derived": [], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_257_1_o1: x as a member of the admitted traffic aggregate; a dev.human_direction with role police_officer, or a dev.traffic_signal not dev.inoperative, governing x's approach carrier or the intersection (dev.governs)."}, {"span": "s2", "atoms": ["dev.stop_sign", "dev.yield_sign", "dev.governs", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "As in NRS_484B_257_1_o1: a dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governing x's approach carrier or the intersection, at x's entry (drv.motion.entering_region)."}, {"span": "s3", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"], "derived": [], "justification": "'vehicle' is the admitted aggregate; 'the driver' is read through its controlled motion."}, {"span": "s10", "atoms": ["rel.occupies", "st.intersection"], "derived": ["drv.motion.entering_region"], "justification": "'shall yield the right-of-way' (DEF-NRS-484A-210 'to proceed ... in preference to another vehicle'): x does not enter the intersection (drv.motion.entering_region over rel.occupies) while a through-highway vehicle is owed precedence."}, {"span": "s11", "atoms": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle", "rel.occupies", "st.intersection", "st.lane_enters", "st.travel_region", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "derived": ["drv.position.entered_via"], "justification": "'other vehicles' are the admitted aggregate. 'which have entered the intersection from such through highway': y occupies the intersection, having entered it through a carrier (drv.position.entered_via, st.lane_enters) that lies on the through highway (st.on_way 'the public way ... a structure region lies on', of kind st.highway) on which x's approach carrier does not lie."}], "operationalizations": [{"span": "s12", "standard": "approaching so closely on the through highway as to constitute an immediate hazard during the time the driver is moving across or within the intersection", "concepts": ["st.region_geometry", "kin.speed", "rel.occupies", "st.lane_enters", "st.on_way", "st.highway"], "params": ["p.immediate_hazard_gap"], "convention": "Gap acceptance (HCM critical headway for a minor-street crossing or turn): a vehicle on an approach carrier of the intersection lying on the through highway (rel.occupies, st.lane_enters, st.on_way), outside the intersection, is an immediate hazard where its ground distance to the intersection (st.region_geometry) is at most its speed (kin.speed) times p.immediate_hazard_gap; the critical gap stands for the time the subject needs to move across or within the intersection, and the bound moves with the other vehicle's proximity and speed.", "surrogate": false}], "assumptions": [], "intentions": [], "compositions": [{"span": "s9", "rule": "NRS_484B_257_1_o1", "map": {"x": "x"}, "as": "compliance"}], "residues": [], "binders": [{"name": "x", "class_elements": ["ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle"]}], "applicability": "As NRS_484B_257_1_o1: x is a vehicle entering intersection i at this observation (drv.motion.entering_region x i) through an approach carrier c it occupies (st.lane_enters c i); a dev.stop_sign or dev.yield_sign governs c or i; x, a member of traffic (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic), is not controlled by a dev.human_direction with role police_officer or a dev.traffic_signal that is not dev.inoperative governing c or i. And NRS_484B_257_1_o1 is complied with for x at this observation (rule NRS_484B_257_1_o1 {x -> x}): that rule being engaged at exactly this entry, its compliance is the fact the words refer to, that x stopped, or under a yield sign slowed or stopped, on this approach.", "obligation": "At this entry, for every highway h2 (st.highway) on which i lies and c does not (st.on_way i h2; st.on_way c h2 false), no vehicle y other than x (ru.aggregate=DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle) either (1) occupies i, having entered it through a carrier c2 that lies on h2 (drv.position.entered_via y i c2, st.lane_enters c2 i, st.on_way c2 h2), or (2) occupies an approach carrier c2 of i lying on h2 (rel.occupies y c2, st.lane_enters c2 i, st.on_way c2 h2), does not occupy i, and st_region_geometry_distance y i is at most kin_speed y times p.immediate_hazard_gap.", "params": ["p.immediate_hazard_gap"], "narrowings": [{"span": "s1", "why": "Control of traffic is read as control of x's own approach or intersection; officer and signal presence are read as their status.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s2", "why": "'proper signs' are read through the presence of a stop or yield sign.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "status"}, {"span": "s3", "why": "'the driver' is read through the vehicle's controlled motion.", "kind": "observable_reading", "category": "agency"}, {"span": "s10", "why": "The yield is judged at x's entry into the intersection.", "kind": "reading"}, {"span": "s12", "why": "'during the time such driver is moving across or within the intersection' is read through the critical gap, not through a prediction of x's own crossing time; 'such through highway' is a highway the intersection lies on and x's signed approach does not.", "kind": "reading"}], "scenarios": [{"name": "forbid", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "dev.stop_sign governs c; x halts at the stop line marking c, then enters i while vehicle y on approach carrier c2 of the crossing highway h2 is 25 m from i at 15 m/s."}, {"name": "permit", "expected": "compliant", "narrative": "As forbid, but x enters i as the only road user in the scene."}, {"name": "idle", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "No sign governs c or i; x enters i."}, {"name": "blind", "expected": "unknown", "narrative": "As forbid, but kin.speed is not observed.", "masked": ["kin.speed"]}, {"name": "branch_1", "expected": "violated", "narrative": "x halts at its stop line and enters i while vehicle y, which entered i through c2 on h2, occupies i."}, {"name": "branch_2", "expected": "not_applicable", "narrative": "As forbid, but x never halted or slowed on the approach (NRS_484B_257_1_o1 not complied with): this duty does not arise."}], "literals": [], "param_proposals": [{"name": "p.immediate_hazard_gap", "unit": "s", "value": 4.1, "convention": "Critical gap: the time within which another road user's arrival at the conflict area, or its predicted closest approach, counts as an immediate hazard to a road user about to cross or join its path.", "source": "HCM 7th ed. Exhibit 20-11 base critical headway (major-street left turn)"}], "gaps": []}
